    "title": "DHS Claim of 16K Noncitizen Voters in Nevada Falls to 0 After State Inquiry - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Chris Walker ,\n1 days ago An estimate from the Department of Homeland Security (DHS) on the number of noncitizen residents registered to vote in Nevada has dropped from an initial claim of nearly 16,000, down to 185, and eventually to zero, just weeks after President Donald Trump cited the claim during a campaign rally in a push to purge several states’ voter rolls. Read full article",
